Exact arithmetic optimization for conditional COUNT23
====================================================
The fixed target, simultaneous contract, p panels, admissible boxes, moment
polygons, count range, quartic choices and acceptance obligations are unchanged.
This named package only changes evaluation of exact rational expressions.
Original count23 source and receipts remain preserved in the parent directory.

Independent algebra review:
1. For the fixed degree-four power-to-Bernstein transform, the change of
   variable coefficient for power j into power i is
   choose(j,i)*lo^(j-i)*(hi-lo)^i. Its sign picks exactly the corresponding
   interval endpoint. The subsequent degree elevation coefficients
   choose(i,j)/choose(4,j) are nonnegative. Summing the selected endpoints is
   therefore exactly the inherited interval calculation. Cached weights are
   indexed by both exact rational phase endpoints, so cannot mix intervals.
2. Multiplication of an interval [l,h] by a point scalar t is [lt,ht] for
   t>=0 and [ht,lt] otherwise. Addition is endpoint addition. The scalar
   helper performs those same operations, delegating non-point products to
   the original method. All modules use the same exact_count_core_v5.I class.
3. At a fixed cubic-moment vertex (x,y), the quartic score differs from its
   interval base only by an affine phase polynomial. Its Bernstein control
   phase is lo+(i/4)*(hi-lo). The respective cubic coefficients are
   mass*(n-k)*(a0-O0-4*phase)/(K*a^4) and
   mass*k*(O1-a1-4*phase)/(K*a^4).
   An exact affine translation commutes with endpoint interval evaluation.
   Taking max over vertices and control indices in either order is identical.
   Positive denominator handling and all early exits retain their old values.

Deployment is explicit in optimized_arithmetic.py: the original exact35_core
is imported, its Bernstein global is replaced, and its joint module refers
to the reviewed affine-translation implementation. The helper also replaces
known imported Bernstein globals. There is no FLOAT discovery import.
The inherited historical leaf token has been renamed PASS_POSITIVE23_TARGET;
this is only a label. The new candidate and receipt schemas name OPTIMIZED_V1.

Fresh check_optimization.py used a separate unmodified parent-directory
Python process for the slow side, then compared70 complete n23 cell output
dictionaries, including positive and empty cells in five different panels.
All were exactly equal. 1,000 deterministic rational quartics also gave
identical upper vectors and minima, including negative phase endpoints, zero widths and
mixed-sign coefficients. CPU time was12.83s versus3.69s (3.48x in this sample).
See OPTIMIZATION_EQUIVALENCE.json for measured values and source hashes.
These checks corroborate the algebra; they do not acquire any resource guard.

Existing candidates may be copied into this namespace with only schema and
historical leaf-label changes. Such candidates are untrusted proposals:
accept_strict.py still reconstructs every closed box, freshly evaluates every
leaf, and runs its negative controls before recording a source-bound receipt.
